// D1586 — a FLOAT REMAINDER's value, delivered everywhere. `%` over two floats was a loud
// check reject (`operator '%' is integer-only, got f64 and f64`); the checker now admits it
// and the emitter lowers it through the once-per-module `__f64_rem__` helper.
//
// The capability is enforced in the CHECKER (one place) and served at every position the
// resulting f64 can be delivered to, which is exactly the shape CLAUDE.md's position-matrix
// rule is about: the helper's RESERVATION is decided by a whole-arena pass reading the node's
// recorded type, so a position whose delivery leaves that type unrecorded would call function
// index -1 — check-clean invalid wasm.
//
// The PROOF multiplies by 2, so a cell that produced an integer remainder (or the truncated
// `a - b * trunc(a / b)` shape at the wrong width) prints something other than 3.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function dividend(): f64 { return 5.5 }
function divisor(): f64 { return 2.0 }
// @@VALUE@@
dividend() % divisor()
// @@TYPE@@
f64
// @@PROOF@@
print(v * 2.0)
// @@WANT@@
3
// @@TEST@@
v > 1.0
// @@HIT@@
print(v * 2.0)
// @@MISS@@
print(0)
// @@VALUE2@@
(0.0 - dividend()) % divisor()
// @@TYPE2@@
f64
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v * 2.0)
// @@WANT2@@
-3
